From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Windows.UI.Xaml hosting -- Application, WindowsXamlManager, Window, DesktopWindowXamlSource

There was no Windows.UI.Xaml at all: XAML Islands programs (NanaZip's file manager, through Mile.Xaml) stopped at RoGetActivationFactory(Windows.UI.Xaml.Application). Our own windows.ui.xaml.dll, its first layer: Application (composable -- an application's App class aggregates it -- Current, RequestedTheme from the system's light/dark setting), WindowsXamlManager.InitializeForCurrentThread (one per thread; gives the thread a hidden CoreWindow and its Window.Current), Window (Current per thread, Bounds, Visible, Content, CoreWindow, events, the private TransparentBackground island hosts set), DesktopWindowXamlSource (composable; AttachToWindow makes the island, a child window of the host; Content; focus events). windows.ui: a thread's CoreWindow (SgCoreWindowForThread) with ICoreWindowInterop, which CoreWindow.GetForCurrentThread returns. Interface definitions (IIDs, method order, parameters) per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and Wine's IDL; IWindowPrivate's IID from Mile.Xaml (MIT); ICoreWindowInterop per windows-rs (MIT). The implementation is ours.
---
